# HydroToxNet

Companion codebase for the paper *HydroToxNet: Forecasting Microcystin Risk in Western Lake Erie Reveals Changing Importance of Nitrogen and Toxin History*.

HydroToxNet is a physics guided spatiotemporal model for forecasting particulate microcystin risk in western Lake Erie at 7, 14, and 21 day horizons. The model combines local ecological conditions, recent toxin history, information from neighboring monitoring stations, and river and meteorological forcing.

All scripts are designed to run in **Google Colab** and expect Google Drive to be mounted at:

`/content/drive/MyDrive/hab_stgnn/`

## Repository Structure

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `data_collection.py` | Collect and merge lake, river, meteorological, and station data into the master dataset |
| `data_preprocessing.py` | Perform weekly aggregation, predictor screening, feature construction, target construction, imputation, and standardization |
| `model.py` | Define the HydroToxNet architecture |
| `model_training.py` | Run hyperparameter search and train the full HydroToxNet model across five random seeds |
| `model_evaluation.py` | Average seed predictions, select validation thresholds, compute evaluation metrics, and run bootstrap significance tests |
| `ablation.py` | Run component ablations and predictor group removal experiments |
| `baseline.py` | Train and evaluate Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost, LSTM, and GAT baselines |
| `model_interpretation.py` | Run grouped permutation importance and annual interpretation analyses |

## Workflow

```text
data_collection.py
        ↓
data_preprocessing.py
        ↓
model_training.py
        ↓
model_evaluation.py
        ↓
├── ablation.py
├── baseline.py
└── model_interpretation.py
